      "explanation": "The doctor consistently identified neurosurgery/urgent care as the responsible pathway, with timing tied to stability versus red flags and then to inpatient surgical planning.",
      "issue_kind": "none",
      "rc_id": "RC4_next_owner_action_timing",
      "status": "met"
    },
    {
      "citations": [
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00200",
          "explanation": "Doctor mentioned perioperative medication questions but did not clearly forbid home mannitol/dehydrating therapy, IV fluids, or antibiotics.",
          "quote": "用镇静/激素/甘露醇？"
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "The doctor did not recommend unsafe home medication, and no family proposal to self-administer was observed, so this is not serious. Still, the authored duty required a clear statement that mannitol/dehydrating therapy, perioperative IV fluids, and perioperative antibiotics were hospital-monitored or preoperative orders and should not be started at home; that explicit correction was absent.",
